        "note": "Padding wastes prefill too: a batch whose longest prompt is 100,000 tokens forces every shorter prompt out to that length, and the layers chew through the padding as text. Continuous batching keeps the linear projections batched but segments attention per sequence with a block-diagonal mask, so finished sequences cost nothing. A decode step at batch one reads one cache; at batch four it reads four caches plus the same weight read.",
