      "id": "pool-admission-split",
      "title": "Each stream's share: 32,768 + 16 + 2 reserved, 32,750 usable",
      "caption": "The 262,144-position KV pool split across four streams gives each 65,536 positions. Admission reserves the 32,768-token reply budget, rounds the batch width up to the 16-row kernel granularity and adds 2 slack positions: 32,768 + 16 + 2. That leaves 65,536 − (32,768 + 16 + 2) = 32,750 positions as the prompt ceiling a request sees. The reservation is a worst-case rule, and a typical request generates 200 tokens against a 32,768-token reservation.",
      "alt": "A horizontal bar of 262,144 positions divided into four equal shares of 65,536. Each share is split into a reserved span of 32,768 reply-budget positions, 16 round rows and 2 slack positions, and an open span of 32,750 positions for the prompt ceiling. The two spans alternate across the bar, so the reserved and usable halves of each stream are visible side by side.",
